Skip grouped quantized CPU Conv1D test when no INT8 GEMM backend is available.

OpenBLAS only provides the floating-point CPU GEMM backend in CTranslate2.
The grouped quantized Conv1D test unconditionally executes an INT8 CPU GEMM,
which fails with "No INT8 GEMM backend for CPU" in builds without MKL,
oneDNN, or Ruy. Skip the test when mayiuse_int8 reports that the selected
device has no supported INT8 GEMM backend.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
--- a/tests/ops_test.cc
+++ b/tests/ops_test.cc
@@ -1238,6 +1238,8 @@ TEST_P(OpDeviceFPTest, Conv1DGroupNoBiasQuantized) {
 #endif
     const Device device = GetParam().device;
     if (device != Device::CPU)
         GTEST_SKIP() << "Grouped quantized convolution is not implemented for CUDA.";
+    if (!mayiuse_int8(device))
+        GTEST_SKIP() << "INT8 GEMM is not available for this device.";
     const DataType dtype = GetParam().dtype;
     const float error = std::max(GetParam().error, float(3e-3));
     const StorageView expected({2, 2, 2}, std::vector<float>{
